mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# SOVEREIGN DAO Economy — Backend API Reference\n\n" #
    "This canister implements the SOVEREIGN DAO & Economy backend: a research-credit ledger, a verified-contribution review workflow, a transparent treasury ledger, a proposed (not deployed) token/emission design, staged DAO governance, and voluntary non-custodial staking bookkeeping. It also exposes the platform authorization scaffold and an Object Query Layer (OQL) `schema()` / `execute()` pair for the Data Intelligence agent.\n\n" #
    "**Nothing in this canister mints, sells, transfers, or custodies a real token or real funds.** SOVEREIGN Research Credits (SRC) are an internal, non-transferable bookkeeping unit — they are not money and do not pay real AI/ICP costs. Treasury figures are admin-entered, never auto-metered. Staking locks only an internal bookkeeping amount, never a real asset; the DAO never takes custody.\n\n" #
    "## Authentication and identity\n\n" #
    "Callers authenticate with Internet Identity. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available, and an agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires — treat it with the same care as a live session.\n\n" #
    "An anonymous (not signed in) caller is always treated as role `#guest` by `getCallerUserRole` — this never traps.\n\n" #
    "## Registration and roles\n\n" #
    "Role-guarded calls require the caller to be **registered** first:\n\n" #
    "1. A signed-in caller must invoke `_initialize_access_control()` once before any role-checked call succeeds for that principal. The platform's Internet Identity integration performs this automatically on sign-in through the app's own frontend; a direct API caller (e.g. a script or a different client) must call it explicitly.\n" #
    "2. The **first** non-anonymous principal ever to call `_initialize_access_control()` becomes `#admin`. Every subsequent new principal becomes `#user`. Calling it again for an already-registered principal is a no-op (idempotent — safe to retry).\n" #
    "3. Calling `_initialize_access_control()` as an anonymous caller traps.\n" #
    "4. A caller can be unregistered even when it legitimately belongs to the app's owner: registration only happens when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so — or a principal derived against a different derivation origin — is a distinct, unregistered principal.\n" #
    "5. `assignCallerUserRole`, `getCallerUserRole`, and `isCallerAdmin` are the unchanged platform access-control endpoints; every DAO economy endpoint below layers its own authorization on top of these roles.\n\n" #
    "Separately from the platform's `#admin` / `#user` / `#guest` roles, `researchCredits` tracks its own **reviewer** flag per principal (`setReviewerRole` / `isCallerReviewer`) — this is independent bookkeeping, not a `UserRole` value, and only an admin can grant or revoke it.\n\n" #
    "## SOVEREIGN Research Credits (SRC) — `researchCredits` domain\n\n" #
    "SRC are earned through admin/reviewer-approved contributions and spent commissioning or prioritizing research assignments. Every registered member (`#user` or `#admin`) can call the member-facing endpoints; only an admin or a reviewer can review contributions; only an admin can advance assignment status or grant/revoke the reviewer flag.\n\n" #
    "- `getCallerSrcBalance() -> Nat` (query, member-only) — the caller's current SRC balance; 0 if the caller has never earned or spent.\n" #
    "- `getCallerSrcTransactions() -> [SrcTransaction]` (query, member-only) — the caller's own full earn/spend history. `reference` links a transaction back to the contribution or assignment that caused it, or `#none`.\n" #
    "- `submitContribution(contributionType, notes, links) -> ContributionId` (update, member-only) — creates a `#pending` contribution. Each call creates a new record; retrying after a network error creates a duplicate submission (not idempotent).\n" #
    "- `getCallerContributions() -> [Contribution]` (query, member-only) — the caller's own submitted contributions at every status.\n" #
    "- `listPendingContributions() -> [Contribution]` (query, reviewer/admin-only) — every contribution still `#pending`.\n" #
    "- `reviewContribution(contributionId, decision, rationale) -> ()` (update, reviewer/admin-only) — `decision` is `#approve(amount : Nat)` (credits `amount` SRC to the contributor and records an `#earn` transaction) or `#reject`. Traps if the contribution was already reviewed or does not exist — reviewing is a one-time transition, so a retry after a genuine success traps; a retry after a network timeout with no state change is safe to repeat.\n" #
    "- `requestAssignment(title, description, srcToSpend, priority) -> AssignmentId` (update, member-only) — spends `srcToSpend` from the caller's balance and creates an assignment in status `#queuedAwaitingFunding`. Traps on insufficient balance.\n" #
    "- `raiseAssignmentPriority(assignmentId, additionalSrc, newPriority) -> ()` (update, requester-only) — spends more SRC to raise the priority of the caller's own still-queued assignment. Traps if not the requester, not queued, or balance insufficient.\n" #
    "- `listAssignments() -> [Assignment]` (query, member-only) — admins/reviewers see every assignment; other members see only their own requests.\n" #
    "- `advanceAssignmentStatus(assignmentId, newStatus) -> ()` (update, admin-only) — moves an assignment through `#queuedAwaitingFunding -> #queued -> #inProgress -> #completed`. The treasury-funding gate (section below) is advisory bookkeeping only — this call does not itself check treasury balance.\n" #
    "- `setReviewerRole(user, isReviewer) -> ()` (update, admin-only) — grants or revokes the reviewer flag for `user`.\n" #
    "- `isCallerReviewer() -> Bool` (query) — true if the caller is an admin or holds the reviewer flag.\n\n" #
    "## Treasury — `treasury` domain\n\n" #
    "A transparent, publicly-readable ledger of real operating funds, kept separate from SRC and from the proposed token supply. Every figure is derived solely from recorded `TreasuryTransaction` entries — nothing is auto-pulled from live ICP cycle balances or AI API usage; all entries are manually admin-entered.\n\n" #
    "- `recordTreasuryTransaction(category, direction, amount, description) -> TreasuryTransaction` (update, admin-only) — appends one entry; amounts are plain `Nat` units chosen by the admin (e.g. whole currency units), there is no implied currency or decimal scaling.\n" #
    "- `listTreasuryTransactions() -> [TreasuryTransaction]` (query, public, no sign-in required) — every entry, newest first.\n" #
    "- `getTreasurySummary() -> TreasurySummary` (query, public) — live-computed totals per category, `totalIncome`, `totalExpense`, a signed `currentBalance` (income minus expense; can be negative), `monthlyOperatingCost` (expenses in the trailing 30 days), and `runwayMonths` (`null` when there is no recent expense history to project from — never means \"infinite runway\"). Every figure is exactly zero until a matching transaction exists.\n\n" #
    "## Proposed tokenomics — `tokenomics` domain\n\n" #
    "**Proposed design only — no token is deployed, minted, sold, or distributed.** Reads are public; writes are admin-only and are rejected outright if the submitted configuration does not exactly respect the fixed 21,000,000 maximum supply.\n\n" #
    "- `getTokenomicsConfig() -> TokenomicsConfig` (query, public) — the fixed `maxSupply` and the current list of `TokenAllocation` entries (category, percentage, exact token amount, vesting/lockup/release/oversight text).\n" #
    "- `updateTokenomicsConfig(allocations) -> Result<(), Text>` (update, admin-only) — replaces the allocation list. Rejected with `#err` unless the submitted percentages sum to exactly 100% and token amounts sum to exactly 21,000,000; never traps for a bad submission, so a caller can retry with a corrected list.\n" #
    "- `getEmissionScheduleConfig() -> EmissionScheduleConfig` (query, public) — the persisted `initialEmission` / `halvingIntervalMonths` plus a freshly recomputed `schedule`: one entry per four-month halving period until emission reaches 0, each with `cumulativeReleased` and `remainingSupply` (floored at 0), always bounded by `maxSupply`. No price, return, or appreciation is implied anywhere in this schedule.\n" #
    "- `updateEmissionSchedule(initialEmission, halvingIntervalMonths) -> Result<(), Text>` (update, admin-only) — recomputes the full schedule for the proposed pair and rejects with `#err` (never traps) if the cumulative total across the displayed periods would exceed `maxSupply`.\n\n" #
    "## DAO governance — `governance` domain\n\n" #
    "Proposal creation, public listing with a live vote tally, one-member-one-vote casting, single-level vote delegation, and admin-only proposal closing. Voting power in this build is a simple one-member-one-vote count — there is no real token-weighted voting live yet.\n\n" #
    "**Safeguard:** token ownership, staking, voting power, or DAO membership never confers Indigenous citizenship, Nation representation, treaty authority, FPIC, or authority over a Nation's legal or political position. This DAO governs only the SOVEREIGN platform and its own resources.\n\n" #
    "- `createProposal(title, description, category) -> ProposalId` (update, member-only) — opens a proposal in status `#open`.\n" #
    "- `listProposals() -> [ProposalView]` (query, public) — every proposal with a live-computed `tally` (counts explicit votes; a member with an active delegation who has not voted directly inherits their delegate's choice — single-level only, no delegation chains).\n" #
    "- `getProposal(id) -> ?ProposalView` (query, public) — `null` if the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `castVote(proposalId, choice) -> ()` (update, member-only) — a later call for the same `(proposalId, caller)` pair overwrites the earlier vote. Traps if the proposal is not `#open`. Idempotent in the sense that re-casting the same choice is harmless, but re-casting a different choice changes the recorded vote.\n" #
    "- `delegateVote(delegate) -> ()` (update, member-only) — sets or replaces the caller's active delegation. Traps on self-delegation.\n" #
    "- `getMyDelegation() -> ?VoteDelegation` (query, member) — the caller's own active delegation, or `null` if none is active.\n" #
    "- `revokeDelegation() -> ()` (update, member-only) — deactivates the caller's delegation if one is active; a no-op otherwise, safe to retry.\n" #
    "- `closeProposal(proposalId) -> ProposalStatus` (update, admin-only) — closes an `#open` proposal as `#passed` or `#rejected` based on the final tally at close time. Traps if already closed.\n\n" #
    "## Voluntary staking — `staking` domain\n\n" #
    "Purely a bookkeeping record of an internal governance-participation amount — the DAO never takes custody of any real asset, mints nothing, and promises no return. A member locks a chosen `Nat` amount against one of a fixed set of published preset lock terms; a longer term accrues a higher proposed maturity rate. This is a proposed, configurable design, not a final parameter set.\n\n" #
    "- `listStakePresets() -> [Preset]` (query, public) — the exact preset `(termSeconds, maturityRateBps, termLabel)` menu that `lockStake` will accept; a `termSeconds` not in this list is rejected.\n" #
    "- `lockStake(amount, termSeconds) -> StakingRecord` (update, registered members only) — creates a new `#active` lock. Traps if the caller is `#guest`, `amount` is 0, or `termSeconds` is not a published preset. `unlockTime` is computed as lock time plus the preset term; there is no early-unlock path.\n" #
    "- `listMyStakes() -> [StakingView]` (query, registered members only) — the caller's own stakes only, newest lock first. Each view reports the stored `status` (`#active` / `#unlocked` only — this mixin never persists `#matured`) alongside a derived `effectiveStatus` that additionally reports `#matured` once `unlockTime` has passed but `unlockStake` has not yet been called, plus a linearly time-accrued `accruedMaturity` and an additive `votingPower = lockedAmount + accruedMaturity`. Both are transparent placeholder figures, not a guarantee of any future reward.\n" #
    "- `unlockStake(id) -> StakingRecord` (update, owner-only) — transitions a stake to `#unlocked`. Traps if the stake does not exist, belongs to a different caller, is already unlocked, or `unlockTime` has not yet passed. Calling it again after a genuine success traps (`already unlocked`); safe to retry after a failed/timed-out call that made no change.\n\n" #
    "## Early access waitlist — `waitlist` domain\n\n" #
    "A simple interest list for the pitch site. Submitting does **not** require sign-in and grants no membership, voting rights, Nation representation or token eligibility. Submissions are stored server-side and are not readable by end users.\n\n" #
    "- `submitWaitlistEntry(name, email, organization, interestArea) -> WaitlistSubmitResult` (update, public, no sign-in required) — validates that `name` and `email` are present and that `email` is well formed, then stores the entry with a server timestamp and returns `#ok(id)`. Returns `#err(#missingName)`, `#err(#missingEmail)`, or `#err(#invalidEmail)` instead of trapping, so a malformed submission can be corrected and retried. Each successful call creates a new record; retrying after a network error creates a duplicate submission (not idempotent). On success it also attempts a confirmation email to the submitter and a notification email to the SOVEREIGN team; a failed email never loses the stored entry and never changes the returned result.\n" #
    "- `listWaitlistEntries() -> [WaitlistEntry]` (query, public) — every stored submission.\n" #
    "- `getWaitlistCount() -> Nat` (query, public) — the number of stored submissions.\n\n" #
    "## Visitor participation experience — `visitor` domain\n\n" #
    "An additive, clearly-labelled demonstration layer on the DAO page. Visitors may participate **anonymously — no sign-in is required** — or optionally sign in with Internet Identity. Nothing here is an official Nation decision, binding vote, or community mandate; every response is a demonstration response.\n\n" #
    "**Privacy:** participation is pseudonymous. A visitor is identified only by a client-generated `sessionId` (an opaque Text the frontend generates and reuses for the browser session); no personal data is collected and no visitor is fingerprinted. An authenticated participant's principal is recorded only when the visitor chooses to sign in, and is `null` for an anonymous visitor.\n\n" #
    "### Public read surface (no sign-in required)\n\n" #
    "- `getWeeklyChallenge() -> ?WeeklyChallenge` (query, public) — the currently active administrator-configured weekly challenge, or `null` when none is configured. `weekKey` is an admin-supplied label (e.g. an ISO week string); `options` is the list of `{ optionId, labelText }` choices.\n" #
    "- `listPublicComments() -> [PublicComment]` (query, public) — publicly visible comments, newest first. Comments whose `moderationStatus` is `#hidden` or `#removed` are never returned.\n\n" #
    "### Public write surface — anonymous participation\n\n" #
    "Every write below accepts an anonymous caller. Each returns a `Result`-style variant (`#ok(id)` / `#err(VisitorError)`) instead of trapping, so a malformed submission can be corrected and retried. Each successful call creates a new record — retrying after a network error creates a duplicate event (not idempotent).\n\n" #
    "- `recordChallengeImpression(sessionId) -> RecordImpressionResult` (update, public) — records that the welcome popup was shown. Returns `#err(#missingSessionId)` when `sessionId` is empty/whitespace.\n" #
    "- `startChallenge(sessionId) -> StartChallengeResult` (update, public) — records that the visitor opened the interactive challenge. Returns `#err(#missingSessionId)` on an empty session id.\n" #
    "- `submitChallengeResponse(sessionId, optionId, reasoning) -> SubmitChallengeResponseResult` (update, public) — records a completed challenge submission. `reasoning` is optional free text. Returns `#err(#missingSessionId)`, `#err(#unknownChallenge)` when no challenge is configured, or `#err(#unknownOption)` when `optionId` is not one of the active challenge's options.\n" #
    "- `submitPublicComment(sessionId, displayName, body) -> SubmitCommentResult` (update, public) — submits a public comment. `displayName` is optional. Returns `#err(#missingSessionId)`, `#err(#missingBody)` for an empty body, or `#err(#bodyTooLong)` when the body exceeds the length limit. New comments start `#visible` and `reported = false`.\n" #
    "- `reportComment(sessionId, commentId, reason) -> ReportCommentResult` (update, public) — reports a comment for administrator review. `reason` is optional. Returns `#err(#missingSessionId)`, `#err(#unknownComment)`, or `#err(#alreadyReported)` when the same session already reported that comment. A successful report also sets the comment's `reported` flag to `true`.\n\n" #
    "### Administrator-only surface — weekly challenge and moderation\n\n" #
    "These require an `#admin` caller. They return `#err(#notAuthorized)` rather than trapping when the caller is not an admin.\n\n" #
    "- `configureWeeklyChallenge(weekKey, question, options) -> ConfigureWeeklyChallengeResult` (update, admin-only) — sets the single active weekly challenge. Returns `#err(#invalidChallenge)` when `weekKey`/`question` is empty, `options` is empty, any option label is empty, or option ids are not unique. Replaces any previously configured challenge.\n" #
    "- `moderateComment(commentId, status) -> ModerateCommentResult` (update, admin-only) — sets a comment's `moderationStatus` to `#visible`, `#hidden`, or `#removed`. Returns `#err(#unknownComment)` when the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `getVisitorAnalytics() -> VisitorAnalytics` (query, admin-only) — the full analytics snapshot. **Traps** with `Unauthorized: Only admins can view visitor analytics` for a non-admin caller. Every figure is derived from recorded events only — never simulated. Includes `totals`, `conversion` (impressions → starts → completions, with percentage rates), `answerDistribution` for the active week, `recentComments`, a daily `weeklyTrend`, and `returningVisitors` (distinct / returning / new sessions).\n\n" #
    "## Lead capture — `visitor` domain (lead pathways)\n\n" #
    "Three separate, clearly-distinguished pathways: **Free Early Access**, **Founding Organization**, and **Strategic Funding Partner**. None of them is a purchase, financial commitment, equity grant, or promise of ownership. Contact details are private and admin-only. Submitting does not require sign-in and grants no membership, voting rights, Nation representation or token eligibility.\n\n" #
    "Each submission validates its input and returns `#ok(id)` / `#err(LeadError)` instead of trapping. `consentToContact` is required for every pathway — follow-up communication is never assumed. Each successful call creates a new lead record (not idempotent). On success the backend also attempts a best-effort confirmation email to the submitter and a notification email to the SOVEREIGN team; a failed send never loses the stored lead and never changes the returned result.\n\n" #
    "- `submitEarlyAccessLead(name, email, organization, organizationType, intendedDaoUseCase, consentToContact) -> SubmitLeadResult` (update, public) — Free Early Access registration. `organization`, `organizationType` and `intendedDaoUseCase` are optional. Returns `#err(#missingName)`, `#err(#missingEmail)`, `#err(#invalidEmail)`, or `#err(#missingConsent)`.\n" #
    "- `submitFoundingOrganizationLead(organization, contactName, email, intendedDeployment, prepaidInterest, budgetRange, consentToContact) -> SubmitLeadResult` (update, public) — Founding Organization expression of interest. `organization` is required (`#err(#missingOrganization)` when empty); `intendedDeployment`, `prepaidInterest` and `budgetRange` are optional. This is an expression of interest, not a purchase or financial commitment.\n" #
    "- `submitStrategicFundingLead(contactName, organization, email, intendedSupport, budgetRange, consentToContact) -> SubmitLeadResult` (update, public) — Strategic Funding Partner inquiry. `organization`, `intendedSupport` and `budgetRange` are optional. An inquiry only — it does not promise equity, returns or ownership.\n\n" #
    "### Administrator-only surface — lead management\n\n" #
    "These require an `#admin` caller. `listLeads` and `getLeadAnalytics` **trap** with `Unauthorized: Only admins can view leads` / `Unauthorized: Only admins can view lead analytics` for a non-admin caller; the update endpoints return `#err(#notAuthorized)` instead.\n\n" #
    "- `listLeads(pathway) -> LeadList` (query, admin-only) — leads for one pathway, newest first, with the pathway's `total`.\n" #
    "- `updateLeadStatus(leadId, status) -> UpdateLeadResult` (update, admin-only) — sets a lead's status to one of `#new`, `#contacted`, `#interested`, `#foundingOrganizationProspect`, `#strategicPartner`, `#converted`, `#notProceeding`. Returns `#err(#unknownLead)` when the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `saveLeadNote(leadId, note) -> UpdateLeadResult` (update, admin-only) — saves a private administrator note (`null` clears it). Returns `#err(#unknownLead)` when the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `getLeadAnalytics() -> LeadAnalytics` (query, admin-only) — aggregate lead counts by pathway, consenting leads, prepaid-interest count, and counts by organization type and status.\n\n" #
    "## Discovery — Collective Intelligence & Collaboration Network — `discovery` domain\n\n" #
    "An additive layer over the DAO economy: a network of communities, ideas, an idea-to-proposal pipeline, opt-in collaboration profiles, mutual-approval introductions, and a real backend-derived activity feed. **AI is advisory only** — it classifies and explains, and never writes governance state. Voting, treasury execution, membership permissions and governance enforcement stay with the existing DAO contracts. Community-level isolation is enforced against each record's `community` field: a community's private submissions, private profile fields and private contact details are never returned to another community.\n\n" #
    "### Submissions\n\n" #
    "- `submitDiscoverySubmission(community, body, category, visibility) -> SubmitDiscoveryResult` (update, member-only) — stores a natural-language idea/feedback/need/opportunity/potential-proposal and returns `#ok({ id, classification })`. The classification is produced by the deterministic keyword/category classifier and is always stored; the advisory inference service is never awaited inline, so a missing or failing inference client never blocks a submission. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)` for a non-member, `#err(#missingBody)` for an empty body, `#err(#bodyTooLong)` when the body exceeds 4000 characters, or `#err(#unknownCommunity)` when the community does not exist. Each successful call creates a new record (not idempotent). A `#publicVisible` submission also appends a public network activity entry.\n" #
    "- `listPublicSubmissions() -> [DiscoverySubmission]` (query, public) — every `#publicVisible` submission across the network.\n" #
    "- `listCommunitySubmissions(community) -> [DiscoverySubmission]` (query, public) — public submissions of that community plus its `#communityOnly` submissions, which are returned only to the community's owner or the submission's author.\n\n" #
    "### Recommendations\n\n" #
    "- `listRecommendations(community) -> [Recommendation]` (query, public) — recommendations for a community, each derived from stored information with a short human-readable `explanation` (for example \"Both communities are exploring renewable energy.\"). Recommendations are never invented activity.\n\n" #
    "### Idea-to-proposal pipeline\n\n" #
    "The visible progression is Idea → Community Feedback → Collaboration → Draft Proposal → Governance Vote → Approved Action → Results. Only a single forward step is allowed at a time.\n\n" #
    "- `createPipelineItem(submissionId, title) -> CreatePipelineItemResult` (update, member-only) — starts a pipeline item from a submission. Only the submission's author or the owning community may start it. Returns `#err(#missingTitle)`, `#err(#unknownSubmission)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `listPipelineItems(community) -> [PipelineItem]` (query, public) — the pipeline items and their stages for a community.\n" #
    "- `advancePipelineItem(itemId, to) -> AdvancePipelineResult` (update, member-only) — advances a pipeline item one stage forward. Only the owning community may advance it. Returns `#err(#unknownPipelineItem)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#invalidStageTransition)` when the requested stage is not the next one.\n" #
    "- `addPipelineInteraction(itemId, kind, body) -> AddInteractionResult` (update, member-only) — records a `#comment`, `#support` or `#improvement` on a pipeline item. Returns `#err(#missingBody)`, `#err(#bodyTooLong)`, `#err(#unknownPipelineItem)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `listPipelineInteractions(itemId) -> [PipelineInteraction]` (query, public) — the interactions recorded on a pipeline item.\n" #
    "- `createProposalFromPipelineItem(itemId) -> CreateProposalFromItemResult` (update, member-only) — creates a formal governance proposal from a pipeline item and returns its `ProposalId`. Only the owning community may do this, and only once per item. The proposal is written into the existing governance `proposals` state, so voting and execution follow the DAO's existing rules. Returns `#err(#unknownPipelineItem)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#invalidStageTransition)` when a proposal already exists for the item.\n\n" #
    "### Directory\n\n" #
    "- `searchDirectory(term, kind) -> [DirectoryEntry]` (query, public) — searches opted-in, publicly visible communities and their published opportunities. `term` is matched case-insensitively against name/description/region and against each published need and partnership opportunity; an empty `term` matches everything. `kind` filters to `#community`, `#opportunity`, or `null` for both.\n\n" #
    "### Community profiles\n\n" #
    "- `saveCommunityProfile(profile) -> SaveCommunityProfileResult` (update, member-only) — creates the caller's community profile on first save and updates it in place afterwards; only the owner may edit an existing profile. If the supplied `profile.id` refers to a profile owned by another principal, the caller's own profile is created under a fresh id instead of being rejected, so any member can always publish their own profile. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#missingTitle)` for an empty name, or `#err(#notAuthorized)` for a non-member.\n" #
    "- `getCommunityProfile(community) -> ?CommunityProfile` (query, public) — the profile, or `null` when it does not exist or is `#privateVisible` and the caller is not its owner.\n\n" #
    "### Collaboration and introductions\n\n" #
    "- `saveCollaborationProfile(profile) -> SaveCollaborationProfileResult` (update, member-only) — publishes or updates the caller's collaboration profile and opt-in flag. A member may only publish a profile for themselves; a community profile may only be published by that community's owner. Returns `#ok(id)` or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `listMatchingCollaborators(community) -> [CollaborationProfile]` (query, public) — opted-in collaboration profiles, excluding the caller's own community.\n" #
    "- `requestIntroduction(target, message) -> RequestIntroductionResult` (update, member-only) — requests an introduction to another party. The requester's approval is implicit at creation; the target must approve before any contact details are shared. Returns `#ok(id)` or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `respondToIntroduction(requestId, approve) -> RespondIntroductionResult` (update, member-only) — the target party approves or declines a pending introduction. Returns `#ok(status)`, `#err(#unknownIntroduction)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)` when the caller is not the target, or `#err(#invalidIntroductionState)` when the request is no longer `#pending`. An approval appends a public partnership activity entry.\n" #
    "- `listMyIntroductions() -> [IntroductionRequest]` (query, public) — introduction requests where the caller is either the requester or the target.\n\n" #
    "### Collective intelligence dashboard\n\n" #
    "- `getCollectiveIntelligenceMetrics() -> CollectiveIntelligenceMetrics` (query, public) — real backend-derived metrics: `activeCommunities`, `ideasSubmitted`, `collaborationOpportunities`, `activeProposals`, `successfulPartnerships`, `completedInitiatives`. Every figure is derived from stored records; empty states are reported as zero, never as fabricated statistics.\n" #
    "- `getNetworkActivityFeed() -> [NetworkActivityEntry]` (query, public) — the interactive feed of real recorded public ideas, proposals, partnerships and community milestones, newest first.\n\n" #
    "## SOVEREIGN OS — Nation workspaces — `sovereign` domain\n\n" #
    "An additive layer over the DAO economy: a sovereign community workspace per Nation, with governance proposals, discussions, members and roles, documents, a calendar, a community treasury, community-controlled privacy settings, an opt-in SOVEREIGN Network listing, and an advisory AI Copilot. **AI is advisory only** — the Copilot answers questions from stored workspace records and never approves a proposal, casts a vote, changes membership or moves treasury funds. Nation-scoped isolation is enforced against each record's `nation` field, and a Nation's workspace content is community-controlled: the per-content privacy settings decide which areas another Nation may read.\n\n" #
    "A built-in demonstration Nation (id `1`, `isSample = true`) is seeded lazily on first read so a visitor always has a workspace to explore without signing in. Every record in it is clearly labelled sample content.\n\n" #
    "### Public read surface (no sign-in required)\n\n" #
    "- `listNations() -> [Nation]` (query, public) — every Nation.\n" #
    "- `getNation(nation) -> ?Nation` (query, public) — `null` if the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `getWorkspace(nation) -> ?Workspace` (query, public) — the Nation's first workspace, or `null` when it has none.\n" #
    "- `listWorkspaceApps(workspace) -> [WorkspaceApp]` (query, public) — the workspace app registry, ordered by `order`. Each app's `status` is `#working` or `#preview`.\n" #
    "- `listNationProposals(nation) -> [NationProposal]` (query, public) — the Nation's own proposals (distinct from the DAO's global governance proposals).\n" #
    "- `getNationProposal(proposal) -> ?NationProposal` (query, public) — `null` if the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `listDiscussionThreads(nation) -> [DiscussionThread]` (query, public) — the Nation's discussion threads.\n" #
    "- `listDiscussionPosts(thread) -> [DiscussionPost]` (query, public) — the posts in a thread.\n" #
    "- `listNationMembers(nation) -> [NationMember]` (query, public) — the Nation's members with their role and permission labels.\n" #
    "- `listNationDocuments(nation) -> [NationDocument]` (query, public) — the Nation's documents.\n" #
    "- `getNationDocument(document) -> ?NationDocument` (query, public) — `null` if the id does not exist.\n" #
    "- `listCalendarEvents(nation) -> [CalendarEvent]` (query, public) — the Nation's calendar events.\n" #
    "- `listNationTreasuryTransactions(nation) -> [NationTreasuryTransaction]` (query, public) — the Nation's treasury entries.\n" #
    "- `getNationTreasurySummary(nation) -> NationTreasurySummary` (query, public) — live-computed `totalIncome`, `totalExpense`, a `balance` floored at zero, and `transactionCount`. Every figure is exactly zero until a matching transaction exists.\n" #
    "- `listGovernanceModelOptions() -> [GovernanceModelOption]` (query, public) — the selectable governance model menu.\n" #
    "- `getRolePermissions(nation) -> [RolePermissionEntry]` (query, public) — the roles-and-permissions matrix (the default matrix when the Nation has not customized it).\n" #
    "- `getPrivacySettings(nation) -> PrivacySettings` (query, public) — the Nation's per-content visibility settings; falls back to the private default when none are saved.\n" #
    "- `listNetworkNations() -> [NetworkNationProfile]` (query, public) — only Nations that opted in to the SOVEREIGN Network.\n\n" #
    "### Interactive sample workflows (no sign-in required for the sample Nation)\n\n" #
    "- `castNationVote(proposal, choice) -> SaveNationProposalResult` (update) — increments the stored tally for `#inFavor` / `#against` / `#abstain`. A visitor may vote on the sample Nation's proposals without signing in; a real Nation's proposals require a signed-in member. Returns `#err(#unknownProposal)` when the id does not exist, or `#err(#notAuthorized)` when the proposal is not `#open` or the caller is not permitted. Each successful call increments the tally (not idempotent).\n" #
    "- `postDiscussionReply(thread, body) -> SaveDiscussionPostResult` (update) — stores a reply and returns `#ok(id)`. A visitor may reply to the sample Nation's threads without signing in; a real Nation's threads require a signed-in member. Returns `#err(#missingBody)`, `#err(#bodyTooLong)` (over 4000 characters), `#err(#unknownThread)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `ensureSampleWorkspace() -> NationId` (update, public) — seeds the built-in demonstration Nation on first call and returns its id. Idempotent: a second call is a no-op.\n\n" #
    "### Nation configuration (signed-in member or administrator)\n\n" #
    "These require a signed-in member of the Nation, or an administrator. They return `#err(#notAuthorized)` rather than trapping when the caller is not permitted.\n\n" #
    "- `saveRolePermissions(nation, entries) -> SavePrivacySettingsResult` (update) — validates that the Nation exists and the caller may configure it. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)` or `#err(#unknownNation)`.\n" #
    "- `savePrivacySettings(settings) -> SavePrivacySettingsResult` (update) — saves the Nation's per-content visibility settings. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)` or `#err(#unknownNation)`.\n" #
    "- `setNetworkOptIn(nation, optIn) -> SetNetworkOptInResult` (update) — sets the SOVEREIGN Network opt-in flag (off by default). Only the Nation's recorded owner or a platform administrator may change it; every other caller receives `#err(#notAuthorized)`. Returns `#err(#unknownNation)` when the Nation does not exist. A confirmed opt-in also syncs the Nation's own `openToCollaboration` flag and `privacyLevel`; an opt-out resets both to private. Idempotent — re-sending the same value is harmless.\n\n" #
    "### Nation OS launcher — five-step creation\n\n" #
    "- `createNationFromLauncher(config) -> CreateNationResult` (update, signed-in member only) — persists a new isolated Nation from the five-step launcher input (`name`, `shortDescription`, `region`, `governanceModelKey`, `membershipVoting`, `selectedApps`, `theme`). The new Nation is **private and not opted in** to the SOVEREIGN Network, and its workspace, selected apps, theme and membership/voting configuration are stored with it. The caller is recorded as the Nation's owner and as its Administrator member. Returns `#ok(nationId)` only after the workspace has actually been saved; a validation failure returns `#err` (`#missingName`, `#missingGovernanceModel`, `#missingApps`, `#invalidTheme`, `#invalidPrivacyLevel`) and never a simulated success. A non-member receives `#err(#notAuthorized)`. Each successful call creates a new Nation (not idempotent).\n" #
    "- `getNationWorkspaceView(nation) -> ?NationWorkspaceView` (query, public) — the Nation's own workspace and settings as one view: the Nation, its first workspace, its apps, its theme, its membership/voting configuration, its privacy settings and its confirmed network opt-in state. `null` when the Nation does not exist.\n" #
    "- `listMyNations() -> [Nation]` (query, signed-in member only) — the Nations the caller is authorized to switch between (the Nations the caller created). Returns `[]` for a non-member.\n" #
    "- `getCollaborationState(nation) -> ?CollaborationState` (query, public) — the Nation's collaboration participation state. `displayLabel` is the honest display string: `\"Private — Not Participating\"` until an authorized administrator confirms opt-in, then `\"Open to Collaboration\"`. A Nation with no confirmed opt-in (including one whose consent state is unknown or missing) reads as not opted in. `null` when the Nation does not exist.\n" #
    "- `getNationTheme(nation) -> NationTheme` (query, public) — the Nation's visual theme (`themeKey`, `wallpaperKey`, `blurEnabled`), falling back to the neutral default when none is saved. Wallpaper preferences are kept separate from governance and identity settings.\n" #
    "- `saveNationTheme(nation, theme) -> SaveNationThemeResult` (update) — saves the Nation's visual theme. Only the Nation's recorded owner or a platform administrator may save it. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#unknownNation)`, or `#err(#invalidTheme)` when `themeKey`/`wallpaperKey` is empty.\n" #
    "- `getMembershipVotingConfig(nation) -> MembershipVotingConfig` (query, public) — the Nation's membership and voting configuration, falling back to the default when none is saved.\n" #
    "- `saveMembershipVotingConfig(nation, config) -> SaveMembershipVotingResult` (update) — saves the Nation's membership and voting configuration. Only the Nation's recorded owner or a platform administrator may save it. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#unknownNation)`, or `#err(#invalidPrivacyLevel)` when a percentage exceeds 100.\n\n" #
    "### AI Copilot — advisory only\n\n" #
    "- `askCopilot(nation, question) -> AskCopilotResult` (update, public) — answers a question about one Nation's workspace from its stored records and returns `#ok(CopilotAnswer)` with the `sources` it drew on and `advisoryOnly = true`. The answer is composed deterministically from stored workspace records; it never approves a proposal, casts a vote, changes membership or moves treasury funds, and it never aborts the update path. Returns `#err(#unknownNation)` or `#err(#missingBody)` for an empty question.\n\n" #
    "## Nation Files — the shared document storage layer — `sovereign` domain\n\n" #
    "Every Nation has its own independent file namespace: a folder tree and file records scoped to exactly one Nation. Files are the central document storage layer — Governance, Documents, Discussions, Projects and Calendar reference the same stored files through attachment links rather than creating duplicate copies. File bytes live off-chain and are referenced by an `ExternalBlob`; the backend stores only that reference, never the bytes. **Both the file metadata and the content reference are access-controlled on the backend** — never by frontend filtering alone. Files are never automatically shared through the regional collaboration network.\n\n" #
    "### Authorization and per-Nation isolation\n\n" #
    "- **Read** (`listNationFolders`, `listNationFiles`, `getNationFileSummary`, `listFileAttachments`) requires a signed-in member of that Nation or a platform administrator. Any visitor may read the built-in sample Nation's files. A caller who is not permitted receives an empty list (or a zeroed summary) rather than an error — the backend never returns another Nation's file metadata.\n" #
    "- **Write** (`createNationFolder`, `renameNationFolder`, `moveNationFolder`, `deleteNationFolder`, `createNationFile`, `renameNationFile`, `moveNationFile`, `deleteNationFile`, `attachFileToTarget`, `detachFile`) requires a signed-in member of that Nation or a platform administrator. Every write returns a `Result`-style variant (`#ok(...)` / `#err(FileError)`) instead of trapping, so a caller can correct and retry.\n" #
    "- **Sample Nation is read-only for every caller.** Any write against the sample Nation returns `#err(#sampleReadOnly)` — anonymous visitors can browse the fictional sample documents but can never modify shared sample records.\n" #
    "- **Cross-Nation access is rejected.** A folder, file or attachment that belongs to a different Nation returns `#err(#crossNationAccess)`; a parent folder or move target must belong to the same Nation. There is no cross-Nation file access without explicit authorization.\n\n" #
    "### Read surface\n\n" #
    "- `listNationFolders(nation) -> [NationFolder]` (query) — the Nation's folders. `parent` is `null` for a root folder.\n" #
    "- `listNationFiles(nation, folder) -> [NationFile]` (query) — the files in one folder; `folder` is `null` for the Nation's root. Each `NationFile` carries `name`, `size` (bytes), `contentType` (MIME), `uploadedBy`, the off-chain `content` reference and a `timestamp`.\n" #
    "- `getNationFileSummary(nation) -> NationFileSummary` (query) — `fileCount`, `folderCount` and `totalBytes` for the Files app header. Every figure is exactly zero when the caller may not read the Nation.\n" #
    "- `listFileAttachments(nation, target) -> [FileAttachment]` (query) — the attachment links for one workspace record. Opening a link resolves the referenced file and respects that file's permissions.\n\n" #
    "### Folder operations\n\n" #
    "- `createNationFolder(nation, parent, name) -> SaveFolderResult` (update) — creates a folder; `parent` is `null` for a root folder. Returns `#err(#missingName)` / `#err(#nameTooLong)` for an invalid name, `#err(#crossNationAccess)` when the parent belongs to another Nation, or `#err(#sampleReadOnly)` / `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `renameNationFolder(nation, folder, name) -> RenameFolderResult` (update) — renames a folder. Returns `#err(#unknownFolder)`, `#err(#crossNationAccess)`, or a name-validation error.\n" #
    "- `moveNationFolder(nation, folder, newParent) -> RenameFolderResult` (update) — moves a folder within the same Nation. Returns `#err(#invalidMove)` when the move would place a folder inside itself or one of its own descendants.\n" #
    "- `deleteNationFolder(nation, folder) -> DeleteFolderResult` (update) — deletes an **empty** folder. Returns `#err(#folderNotEmpty)` when the folder still contains files or subfolders.\n\n" #
    "### File operations\n\n" #
    "- `createNationFile(nation, folder, name, size, contentType, content) -> SaveFileResult` (update) — registers an uploaded file's metadata and off-chain content reference. `content` is the `ExternalBlob` returned by the object-storage upload; the bytes are never stored on-chain. Returns `#err(#duplicateName)` when a file of the same name already exists in that folder, `#err(#crossNationAccess)` when the folder belongs to another Nation, or a name-validation error.\n" #
    "- `renameNationFile(nation, file, name) -> SaveFileResult` (update) — renames a stored file. Returns `#err(#unknownFile)`, `#err(#crossNationAccess)`, `#err(#duplicateName)`, or a name-validation error.\n" #
    "- `moveNationFile(nation, file, folder) -> MoveFileResult` (update) — moves a file to another folder of the same Nation; `folder` is `null` for the root. Returns `#err(#duplicateName)` when the target folder already holds a file of that name.\n" #
    "- `deleteNationFile(nation, file) -> DeleteFileResult` (update) — deletes a file **and every attachment link that referenced it**. Returns `#err(#unknownFile)` or `#err(#crossNationAccess)`.\n\n" #
    "### Attachments — one shared document system\n\n" #
    "An attachment is a link from a workspace record to an existing stored file; it carries no copy of the file. `FileAttachmentTarget` is one of `#proposal(id)`, `#discussionPost(id)`, `#project(id)`, `#calendarEvent(id)` or `#document(id)`.\n\n" #
    "- `attachFileToTarget(nation, file, target) -> SaveAttachmentResult` (update) — links an existing stored file to a workspace record. Returns `#err(#unknownFile)` or `#err(#crossNationAccess)`.\n" #
    "- `detachFile(nation, attachment) -> DeleteFileResult` (update) — removes an attachment link; the stored file itself is not deleted. Returns `#err(#unknownAttachment)` or `#err(#crossNationAccess)`.\n\n" #
    "### Nation Files errors\n\n" #
    "`FileError` is one of `#missingName`, `#nameTooLong`, `#unknownNation`, `#unknownFolder`, `#unknownFile`, `#unknownAttachment`, `#unknownTarget`, `#notAuthorized`, `#notNationMember`, `#folderNotEmpty`, `#duplicateName`, `#invalidMove`, `#crossNationAccess`, or `#sampleReadOnly`. Every Files mutation returns one of these instead of trapping, so a caller can correct and retry. Each successful create call allocates a new id (not idempotent); a retry after a network error creates a duplicate record.\n\n" #
    "## DAO Constitution & Governance — `constitution`, `roles`, `execution` and `census` domains\n\n" #
    "An additive layer over the Nation workspace: each Nation defines its own constitution (a versioned governance policy), its roles and delegations, its governance proposals and votes, its execution requests, its appeals and its Participation Census. **The DAO governs; the OS is the interface.** Every record is Nation-scoped and private by default: a Nation's governance records are never readable by another Nation, and the templates are examples, not assumptions about an organization's legal or traditional governance authority.\n\n" #
    "### Constitution — `constitution` domain\n\n" #
    "A Nation's constitution is a versioned governance policy. Before activation a Nation is in **Founding Setup**; after activation, rules change only through a constitutionally authorized amendment — a direct rule edit on an activated Nation is rejected. Historical decisions are preserved under the rules effective when those decisions occurred.\n\n" #
    "- `listConstitutionTemplates() -> [GovernanceModelOption]` (query, public) — the six editable templates (Indigenous Nation, Nonprofit, Cooperative, Business, Community, Custom DAO). Each is an example starting point, not a claim about an organization's authority.\n" #
    "- `getDefaultRuleSet(templateKey) -> GovernanceRuleSet` (query, public) — the default rule set for a template. Every setting is a plain configurable value the organization may change before activation.\n" #
    "- `validateGovernanceRuleSet(rules) -> ?GovernanceError` (query, public) — validates a submitted rule set; returns the first validation error, or `null` when acceptable.\n" #
    "- `getActiveConstitution(nation) -> ?Constitution` (query) — the active constitution and its rule set. Only a member of that Nation (or an administrator) may read it; any visitor may read the sample Nation's. Returns `null` when the caller may not read it or the Nation has no active constitution.\n" #
    "- `getActiveRuleSet(nation) -> ?GovernanceRuleSet` (query) — the active rule set, or `null` when the Nation has no active constitution or the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `listAmendments(nation) -> [Amendment]` (query) — the Nation's amendment history, ordered by resulting version. Each amendment records the rules in effect before and after it. Returns `[]` when the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `getFoundingSetup(nation) -> ?FoundingSetup` (query) — the founding setup state, or `null` when the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `listFoundingAppointments(nation) -> [FoundingAppointment]` (query) — the Nation's founding appointments. Returns `[]` when the caller may not read them.\n" #
    "- `beginFoundingSetup(nation) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, Nation owner or admin) — begins founding setup. Idempotent: a second call is a no-op once a setup exists. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)` or `#err(#unknownNation)`.\n" #
    "- `appointFoundingAuthority(nation, authority, appointmentLabel) -> SaveConstitutionResult` (update, founding authority or admin) — appoints a founding authority while in Founding Setup. Each authority independently accepts through Internet Identity. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, or `#err(#missingName)`.\n" #
    "- `acceptFoundingAppointment(nation, appointment) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, appointed authority only) — accepts an appointment. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, or `#err(#unknownConstitution)`.\n" #
    "- `declineFoundingAppointment(nation, appointment) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, appointed authority only) — declines an appointment. A declined appointment can be replaced.\n" #
    "- `replaceFoundingAppointment(nation, appointment, newAuthority, appointmentLabel) -> SaveConstitutionResult` (update, founding authority or admin) — replaces a declined or expired appointment. Returns `#ok(id)` or an error.\n" #
    "- `cancelFoundingSetup(nation) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, founding authority or admin) — cancels a setup before activation; no private organizational access is granted.\n" #
    "- `saveConstitution(nation, templateKey, rules) -> SaveConstitutionResult` (update, founding authority or admin, Founding Setup only) — validates and stores a confirmed constitution. Saving a new version supersedes the previous one, which is kept as history. Returns `#ok(id)` or a validation/authorization error.\n" #
    "- `activateFounding(nation) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, founding authority or admin) — activates a Nation only after its founding authorities have accepted and an active confirmed constitution exists. Returns `#err(#alreadyActivated)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, `#err(#unknownConstitution)`, or `#err(#notFoundingAuthority)`.\n" #
    "- `amendConstitution(nation, summary, newRules) -> SaveAmendmentResult` (update, founding authority or admin, activated Nations only) — amends an activated Nation's constitution, recording the rules before and after. Returns `#ok(amendmentId)` or an error.\n\n" #
    "### Founding-seat confirmation & launch status\n\n" #
    "The creator's **Founding Authority #1** seat is recorded when the Nation is created, so the creator confirms that same seat instead of appointing a second one. The three-distinct-authority activation requirement and the Pending Activation state are unchanged.\n\n" #
    "- `confirmFoundingSeat(nation, appointment) -> ConfirmFoundingSeatResult` (update, the seat's own authority only) — confirms the caller's existing pending seat in place. Confirming an already-accepted seat is a no-op that returns `#ok(appointment)`. Returns `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)` when the setup is not in Founding Setup or the seat is not pending, `#err(#unknownConstitution)` for an unknown appointment, `#err(#notAuthorized)` when the seat belongs to another principal, carries an invitation token, or the caller already holds another seat, or `#err(#setupExpired)` when the seat has expired.\n" #
    "- `getLaunchStatus(nation) -> ?LaunchStatus` (query, Nation owner or admin) — the launch status: `setupStatus`, `lifecycleState`, `acceptedAuthorities` out of `requiredAuthorities` (three), `callerSeats`, `awaitingOtherSeats`, `constitutionSaved`, `canResume`, and a plain-language `blockedReason` (empty when the launch can continue). Returns `null` when the caller is not the Nation's owner or an administrator.\n" #
    "- `resumeLaunch(nation) -> ResumeLaunchResult` (update, Nation owner or admin) — reports the current launch status so the caller can continue from the first unfinished step. It never creates a duplicate Nation and never re-runs a saved step. Returns `#ok(LaunchStatus)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#unknownNation)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpiredRecoverable)` when the setup window has expired, or `#err(#setupCancelledRecoverable)` when the setup was cancelled — in both recoverable cases the creator can start a fresh founding setup for the same Nation.\n\n" #
    "### Roles & permissions — `roles` domain\n\n" #
    "Ten built-in governance roles (Founding Authority, Membership Authority, Member, Governance Delegate, Proposal Steward, Execution Authority, Treasury Steward, Document Steward, Auditor, Observer) plus custom roles. Permissions are scoped across view, propose, approve, vote, modify and execute. A member may hold multiple roles; a delegation carries an expiry and can be revoked. **Permissions are enforced in the canister, not by frontend controls alone.**\n\n" #
    "- `listNationRoles(nation) -> [GovernanceRole]` (query) — the Nation's role definitions.\n" #
    "- `ensureNationRoles(nation) -> [GovernanceRole]` (update) — seeds the built-in roles for a Nation if not already present; idempotent.\n" #
    "- `getNationRole(nation, role) -> ?GovernanceRole` (query) — one role definition, or `null`.\n" #
    "- `listRoleAssignments(nation) -> [RoleAssignment]` (query) — the Nation's role assignments.\n" #
    "- `listRoleDelegations(nation) -> [RoleDelegation]` (query) — the Nation's role delegations.\n" #
    "- `getCallerCapabilities(nation) -> [GovernanceCapability]` (query) — the capabilities the caller holds in that Nation.\n" #
    "- `callerHasCapability(nation, capability) -> Bool` (query) — whether the caller holds one capability in that Nation.\n" #
    "- `getMembershipApprovalStatus(nation, member) -> { approvals : Nat; required : Nat }` (query) — how many approvals a member has and how many are required.\n" #
    "- `createCustomRole(nation, roleName, description, capabilities) -> SaveRoleResult` (update, authorized member) — creates a custom role within platform security constraints. The role's capabilities must be a subset of the caller's own, so a caller can never grant a capability it does not hold.\n" #
    "- `updateRoleCapabilities(nation, role, capabilities) -> SaveRoleResult` (update, authorized member) — updates a role's capabilities.\n" #
    "- `assignRole(nation, member, role) -> SaveRoleAssignmentResult` (update, authorized member) — assigns a role to a member.\n" #
    "- `revokeRole(nation, assignment) -> SaveRoleAssignmentResult` (update, authorized member) — revokes a role assignment.\n" #
    "- `createRoleDelegation(nation, delegate, role, capabilities, expiresAt) -> SaveRoleDelegationResult` (update, authorized member) — creates a scoped delegation with an expiry.\n" #
    "- `revokeRoleDelegation(nation, delegation) -> SaveRoleDelegationResult` (update, authorized member) — revokes a delegation before it expires.\n" #
    "- `approveMembership(nation, member) -> MembershipApprovalResult` (update, authorized member) — records one approval; the member is admitted once the Nation's approval threshold is reached. Returns `#ok({ approvalId, admitted })` or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n\n" #
    "### Decisions — `execution` domain (governance proposals and votes)\n\n" #
    "A governance proposal carries its classification, review and discussion periods, quorum, thresholds, abstentions and ties. **Passing a vote never implies execution.** Confidential votes are counted but their voter is withheld from public reads.\n\n" #
    "- `createGovernanceProposal(nation, title, summary, classification, reviewPeriodDays, discussionPeriodDays, quorumPercent, approvalThresholdPercent, abstentionsCount, tieBreakRule) -> SaveGovernanceProposalResult` (update, authorized member) — creates a proposal in `#draft`.\n" #
    "- `listGovernanceProposals(nation) -> [GovernanceProposal]` (query) — the Nation's proposals.\n" #
    "- `getGovernanceProposal(proposal) -> ?GovernanceProposal` (query) — one proposal by id, or `null`.\n" #
    "- `castGovernanceVote(proposal, choice, confidential) -> SaveGovernanceProposalResult` (update, eligible member) — casts a vote; a later call for the same `(proposal, caller)` pair overwrites the earlier vote.\n" #
    "- `closeGovernanceProposal(proposal) -> SaveGovernanceProposalResult` (update, authorized member) — closes voting and records the outcome (`#approved`, `#rejected`, `#noQuorum`, or `#tied`).\n\n" #
    "### Safe proposal execution — `execution` domain\n\n" #
    "Execution is a separate request, manually authorized by default. High-risk actions (treasury transfers, constitutional changes, authority changes and destructive actions) require independent authorization; a timelock delays execution; an emergency pause blocks it; every state change is recorded in an audit trail. Unauthorized, duplicate or modified execution requests are rejected.\n\n" #
    "- `requestExecution(proposal) -> SaveExecutionRequestResult` (update, authorized member) — creates an execution request in `#pendingAuthorization` for a proposal that has passed.\n" #
    "- `authorizeExecution(request) -> SaveExecutionRequestResult` (update, execution authority) — authorizes a pending request; a high-risk request requires independent authorization. Returns `#err(#notAuthorized)` or `#err(#unknownExecutionRequest)`.\n" #
    "- `executeRequest(request) -> SaveExecutionRequestResult` (update, execution authority) — executes an authorized request once its timelock has passed. Rejects unauthorized, duplicate or modified requests.\n" #
    "- `cancelExecution(request) -> SaveExecutionRequestResult` (update, authorized member) — cancels a request before execution.\n" #
    "- `setExecutionPaused(nation, paused) -> SaveExecutionRequestResult` (update, authorized member) — sets the emergency pause for a Nation's execution queue.\n" #
    "- `listExecutionRequests(nation) -> [ExecutionRequest]` (query) — the Nation's execution requests.\n" #
    "- `getExecutionRequest(request) -> ?ExecutionRequest` (query) — one request by id, or `null`.\n" #
    "- `listExecutionAudit(request) -> [ExecutionAuditEntry]` (query) — the audit trail for one execution request.\n\n" #
    "### Appeals, disputes and recusal — `execution` domain\n\n" #
    "Appeals cover membership rejection, inactivity and governance decisions. An appeal carries evidence and a recusal record for any reviewer with a conflict of interest.\n\n" #
    "- `fileAppeal(nation, kind, subjectId, summary) -> SaveAppealResult` (update, member) — files an appeal in `#submitted`.\n" #
    "- `addAppealEvidence(appeal, evidenceLabel, detail) -> SaveAppealResult` (update, member) — attaches one piece of evidence.\n" #
    "- `recuseFromAppeal(appeal, reason) -> SaveAppealResult` (update, reviewer) — records a reviewer's recusal for a documented conflict of interest.\n" #
    "- `decideAppeal(appeal, uphold, decisionNote) -> SaveAppealResult` (update, authorized member) — decides an appeal as upheld or denied.\n" #
    "- `listAppeals(nation) -> [Appeal]` (query) — the Nation's appeals.\n" #
    "- `getAppeal(appeal) -> ?Appeal` (query) — one appeal by id, or `null`.\n\n" #
    "### Participation Census — `census` domain\n\n" #
    "A privacy-aware governance accountability record: who is eligible, who participates, what decisions are made and whether approved actions are executed. Confidential votes are recorded as participation without exposing the choice; historical records are preserved after membership or authority changes.\n\n" #
    "- `listCensusEntries(nation) -> [CensusEntry]` (query) — the Nation's census entries. Entries marked `confidential` are returned with their detail redacted.\n" #
    "- `getCensusSummary(nation) -> CensusSummary` (query) — the accountability summary: `eligibleMembers`, `activeMembers`, `proposals`, `votes`, `delegations`, `disputes` and `executions`. Confidential entries contribute to the counts without exposing their detail.\n" #
    "- `recordCensusEntry(nation, kind, subject, referenceId, summary, confidential, constitutionVersion) -> RecordCensusResult` (update, authorized member) — records one census entry. Returns `#ok(id)` or an error.\n\n" #
    "## Constitutional enforcement — founding authorities, membership onboarding and voting eligibility\n\n" #
    "Every DAO governs itself through its own constitution, not through the discretion of its creator or a platform administrator. The endpoints below enforce that in the backend: founding activation, membership approval thresholds, voting eligibility and the auditable governance history are all validated server-side, never by the UI alone. Every record is Nation-scoped and private by default — a Nation's onboarding and governance records are never readable by another Nation.\n\n" #
    "### Founding authorities and activation\n\n" #
    "A Nation starts in **Founding Setup** and stays **Pending Activation** until three distinct authenticated principals have accepted a founding appointment and an active confirmed constitution exists. Activation is automatic — there is no manual administrator bypass.\n\n" #
    "- `getFoundingStatus(nation) -> { accepted : Nat; required : Nat; activated : Bool }` (query) — the founding acceptance status: how many distinct authorities have accepted out of the required three, and whether the Nation is Active. A caller who may not read the Nation's constitution receives `{ accepted = 0; required = 3; activated = false }` rather than an error.\n" #
    "- `inviteFoundingAuthority(nation, invitedEmail, appointmentLabel) -> SaveConstitutionResult` (update, founding authority or admin, Founding Setup only) — appoints a founding authority by secure email invitation. The invitation token is single-use and bound to the accepting principal; until accepted the seat is held by a placeholder principal so it cannot be double-appointed. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, or `#err(#missingName)` for an empty label or email.\n" #
    "- `acceptFoundingInvitation(nation, token) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, any signed-in caller holding the token) — accepts an invitation appointment through its single-use token. The token binds the seat to the caller principal and is consumed on acceptance; an expired, already-consumed, or unknown token is rejected. The same principal can never hold two founding seats. Returns `#ok` (and activates automatically when the third distinct authority accepts and a constitution exists), `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `acceptFoundingAppointment(nation, appointment) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, the appointed principal only) — accepts a direct (non-invitation) appointment. An invitation appointment must be accepted through `acceptFoundingInvitation` instead. Returns `#ok`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, `#err(#setupExpired)`, or `#err(#unknownConstitution)`.\n" #
    "- `activateFounding(nation) -> ActivateFoundingResult` (update, founding authority or admin) — reports the current activation state and activates only when the founding requirements are already satisfied; it never forces activation. Returns `#ok` when already active, or `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`.\n" #
    "- `listGovernanceHistory(nation) -> [GovernanceHistoryEntry]` (query) — the append-only per-Nation governance history: appointments, acceptances, approvals, rejections, votes and amendments. Returns `[]` when the caller may not read it.\n\n" #
    "### Membership onboarding — join requests and invitations\n\n" #
    "Workflow: Request → Pending Review → Required Approvals → Role Assignment → Active Membership. The required number of distinct authorized approvals is derived from the Nation's active constitution (a configurable percentage of eligible approvers, rounded up, never below the default of three) and is captured when the request is created, so a later constitutional change never applies retroactively. Each authorized approver is counted once; self-approval and duplicate membership are prevented.\n\n" #
    "- `submitJoinRequest(nation, displayName, message) -> SubmitJoinRequestResult` (update, signed-in caller) — creates a `#pendingReview` join request. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#missingName)` for an empty display name, or `#err(#notAuthorized)` when the caller is already a member or already has an open request. Each successful call creates a new record (not idempotent).\n" #
    "- `reviewJoinRequest(nation, request, approve) -> ReviewJoinRequestResult` (update, caller holding the `#approve` capability) — records one distinct authorized approval, or rejects the request. The applicant may never approve its own request, and each approver counts once. Once the captured required approvals are reached the request moves to `#approved` and the applicant is admitted as `#active`. Returns `#ok(status)` (`#underReview`, `#approved`, `#active`, `#rejected`, or `#expired`), `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#unknownProposal)` for an unknown request id.\n" #
    "- `withdrawJoinRequest(nation, request) -> ReviewJoinRequestResult` (update, the applicant only) — withdraws the caller's own open request. Returns `#ok(#withdrawn)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#unknownProposal)`.\n" #
    "- `listJoinRequests(nation) -> [JoinRequest]` (query) — the Nation's join requests. Returns `[]` when the caller is not a member of the Nation.\n" #
    "- `issueMembershipInvitation(nation, invitedEmail) -> IssueInvitationResult` (update, caller holding the `#approve` capability) — issues a secure membership invitation with a single-use token and a 14-day expiry window. Returns `#ok(id)` or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `acceptMembershipInvitation(nation, token) -> AcceptInvitationResult` (update, any signed-in caller holding the token) — accepts an invitation through its single-use token, binding the acceptance to the caller principal and admitting the caller as an active member. Returns `#ok(admissionId)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)` for an unknown or already-consumed token, or `#err(#setupExpired)` for an expired token.\n\n" #
    "### Voting eligibility and recorded votes\n\n" #
    "Voting eligibility is validated in the backend before a vote is accepted. A member must have served the default 8-day waiting period after admission and must have qualifying activity (a recorded vote, a governance proposal, or a filed appeal) within the 30-day activity window. Eligibility rules apply consistently, so a new community is never penalized indefinitely.\n\n" #
    "- `getVotingEligibility(nation) -> VotingEligibility` (query) — the caller's eligibility: `eligible`, a `restriction` (`#waitingPeriod`, `#inactivity`, `#notAdmitted`, or `null` when eligible), and `eligibleFrom` (when the waiting period ends, if still in it).\n" #
    "- `castGovernanceVote(proposal, choice, confidential) -> SaveGovernanceProposalResult` (update, eligible Nation member) — records one vote per member per decision. A second vote on the same decision is rejected with `#err(#alreadyVoted)`; an ineligible member receives `#err(#notAuthorized)`. Returns `#ok(proposalId)` on success.\n" #
    "- `listRecordedVotes(nation, decision) -> [RecordedVote]` (query) — the recorded votes for one decision. A confidential vote's voter is withheld (reported as the anonymous principal). Returns `[]` when the caller is not a member of the Nation.\n\n" #
    "## Member departure and emergency governance — `departure` domain\n\n" #
    "Voluntary departure, retirement, suspension and constitutional removal, plus restricted emergency suspension and its restoration. **When a departure becomes effective, the member's operational permissions are revoked immediately** — every role assignment is removed, every delegation to or from the member is deactivated, and the member is removed from the Nation's roster. Historical contributions and governance records (census entries, recorded votes, governance history) are never deleted. A voluntary departure or retirement is the member's own act and may become effective immediately; a suspension or constitutional removal is involuntary and must pass through notice, review and an appeal path before it becomes final. Every record is Nation-scoped and private by default.\n\n" #
    "- `recordMemberDeparture(nation, member, kind, notice) -> SaveMemberDepartureResult` (update) — records a departure. A member may record its own `#voluntaryDeparture` or `#retirement` (effective immediately); a caller holding the `#modify` capability may record a `#suspension` or `#constitutionalRemoval` (starts in `#notice`, never effective on this call). Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#missingReason)` for an empty or over-long notice, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#selfApproval)` when a caller tries to remove itself involuntarily, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when the Nation is archived or the member already has an effective departure.\n" #
    "- `reviewMemberDeparture(nation, departure, reviewNote) -> SaveMemberDepartureResult` (update, `#modify` capability) — records the review outcome of an involuntary departure and moves it to `#underReview`. The member may never review its own departure. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#unknownDeparture)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#selfApproval)`, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)`.\n" #
    "- `finalizeMemberDeparture(nation, departure) -> SaveMemberDepartureResult` (update, `#modify` capability) — makes an involuntary departure effective once it has been reviewed and its review window has elapsed, revoking the member's permissions immediately. A departure still in `#notice` or still inside its review window cannot be finalized. Returns `#ok(id)` or an error.\n" #
    "- `withdrawMemberDeparture(nation, departure) -> SaveMemberDepartureResult` (update) — withdraws a departure before it becomes effective. The member may withdraw its own; an authorized administrator may withdraw any open one. Returns `#ok(id)` or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when already effective.\n" #
    "- `appealMemberDeparture(nation, departure, summary) -> SaveMemberDepartureResult` (update, the departing member only) — files an appeal against an involuntary departure before it becomes effective; the departure moves to `#appealed`. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#missingSummary)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)`.\n" #
    "- `listMemberDepartures(nation) -> [MemberDeparture]` (query) — the Nation's departures. A member of the Nation (or an administrator) reads all; a departing member always reads its own. Returns `[]` otherwise.\n" #
    "- `getMemberDeparture(departure) -> ?MemberDeparture` (query) — one departure by id, or `null` when the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `isMemberDeparted(nation, member) -> Bool` (query) — whether a member has an effective departure. Returns `false` when the caller is not a member of the Nation.\n" #
    "- `exportMyRecords(nation) -> PersonalRecordExport` (query) — the caller's own authorized personal records for one Nation: its admission record, census entries, recorded votes and departures. Scoped to the caller; a caller can never export another member's records.\n\n" #
    "### Emergency governance\n\n" #
    "A restricted emergency suspension for suspected account compromise, unauthorized activity or governance integrity threats. It requires **two of three authorized authorities by default**, carries a defined expiry (72 hours), and is narrowly scoped. **Emergency powers can never amend the constitution, seize assets, permanently remove authorities or dissolve the Nation** — a request whose affected functions name any of those is rejected with `#err(#emergencyScopeExceeded)`.\n\n" #
    "- `requestEmergencySuspension(nation, reason, affectedAccounts, affectedFunctions) -> SaveEmergencySuspensionResult` (update, an authorized authority — the Nation's owner, a member holding a role with the `#approve` capability, or a platform administrator) — requests a suspension; the caller's own approval is recorded. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#missingReason)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#emergencyScopeExceeded)`, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when the Nation is archived.\n" #
    "- `approveEmergencySuspension(nation, suspension) -> SaveEmergencySuspensionResult` (update, authorized authority) — records one distinct authority's approval; each authority counts once. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#duplicateApproval)`, `#err(#unknownSuspension)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)`.\n" #
    "- `restoreEmergencySuspension(nation, suspension, note) -> RestoreEmergencySuspensionResult` (update, `#modify` capability) — records the restoration, returns the Nation to Active when it was temporarily suspended, and appends to the suspension's audit trail. Returns `#ok` or an error.\n" #
    "- `listEmergencySuspensions(nation) -> [EmergencySuspension]` (query) — the Nation's emergency suspensions. Returns `[]` when the caller is not a member of the Nation.\n" #
    "- `getEmergencySuspension(suspension) -> ?EmergencySuspension` (query) — one suspension by id, or `null` when the caller may not read it.\n\n" #
    "## DAO lifecycle & constitutional continuity — `constitution`, `departure` and `dissolution` domains\n\n" #
    "The constitution must outlive its founders. Authority positions are separated from the individuals occupying them, and every continuity action is decided by the backend against the Nation's lifecycle state — the interface only reflects it. **No individual, founding authority, platform administrator or developer has unilateral control over an activated DAO.** Every record is Nation-scoped and private by default: only a member of that Nation (or a platform administrator) may read its continuity records, and any visitor may read the built-in sample Nation's. Every read below returns `null` / `[]` / a zeroed view rather than an error when the caller may not read it; every mutation returns a `Result`-style variant (`#ok(...)` / `#err(LifecycleError)`) instead of trapping.\n\n" #
    "### Lifecycle states\n\n" #
    "A Nation is in exactly one backend-enforced state: `#draft`, `#pendingActivation`, `#active`, `#restrictedGovernance`, `#temporarilySuspended`, `#pendingDissolution` or `#archived`. The effective state is derived from the Nation's founding setup unless a stored overriding state is in force. Each state permits a defined set of actions; an action not permitted in the current state is rejected with `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` or `#err(#notAuthorized)`. An `#archived` Nation has operational governance disabled while its authorized history is preserved.\n\n" #
    "- `getNationLifecycle(nation) -> ?{ state, stateKey, explanation, enteredAt, reason }` (query) — the current lifecycle state with a plain-language explanation. `null` when the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `getActivationRequirements(nation) -> { accepted, required, hasConfirmedConstitution, constitutionRatifiedByAll, planRatified, outstanding }` (query) — what is still needed before activation. `required` is the number of founding authorities (three); `outstanding` lists the remaining requirements in plain language.\n\n" #
    "### Authority succession and replacement\n\n" #
    "An authority position persists across holders; the holder is optional so a position can be vacant without losing its history. A successor must accept independently through their own Internet Identity principal — authority is never transferred automatically from inactivity, an email request or an unverified report of death.\n\n" #
    "- `listAuthorityPositions(nation) -> [AuthorityPosition]` (query) — the Nation's authority positions with their seat label, term, current holder (or `null` when vacant) and status (`#vacant` / `#filled` / `#suspended` / `#retired`).\n" #
    "- `listAuthorityTermEvents(nation) -> [AuthorityTermEvent]` (query) — the permanent appointment, acceptance, resignation, retirement, replacement and removal history, ordered by id.\n" #
    "- `createAuthorityPosition(nation, seatLabel, termStart, termEnd) -> SaveAuthorityPositionResult` (update, founding authority or administrator) — creates a vacant position. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#unknownNation)`, `#err(#missingReason)` for an empty seat label, or a lifecycle error.\n" #
    "- `appointAuthoritySuccessor(nation, position, successor, successorDisplayLabel, reason) -> RecordAuthorityTermEventResult` (update, founding authority or administrator) — records an appointment and leaves the position vacant until the successor accepts. Returns `#ok(eventId)`, `#err(#unknownPosition)`, `#err(#duplicateIdentity)` when the principal already holds another position in the Nation, `#err(#missingReason)`, or a lifecycle error.\n" #
    "- `acceptAuthorityAppointment(nation, position) -> RecordAuthorityTermEventResult` (update, the appointed successor only) — the successor accepts through their own principal, filling the position. Returns `#ok(eventId)`, `#err(#unknownPosition)`, or `#err(#notAuthorized)` when the caller is not the most recently appointed successor.\n" #
    "- `recordAuthorityDeparture(nation, position, kind, reason) -> RecordAuthorityTermEventResult` (update) — records a `#resignation`, `#retirement`, `#replacement` or `#removal`. A resignation or retirement may only be recorded by the position's own holder; a replacement or removal requires the founding authority. The position becomes vacant; the holder is never transferred automatically. Returns `#ok(eventId)`, `#err(#unknownPosition)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#missingReason)`, or a lifecycle error.\n\n" #
    "### Succession and recovery plan\n\n" #
    "A viable succession and recovery plan must be ratified by every founding authority before a Nation activates. Recovery procedures remain functional if one, two or all three authorities become unavailable, and approval thresholds are never silently reduced when an authority leaves.\n\n" #
    "- `getSuccessionPlan(nation) -> ?SuccessionRecoveryPlan` (query) — the plan: designated successors, alternate authorities, the elected membership council, independent recovery trustees, the recovery approval threshold, the identity recovery procedure, and one ratification per founding authority. `null` when none exists or the caller may not read it.\n" #
    "- `saveSuccessionPlan(nation, plan) -> SaveSuccessionPlanResult` (update, founding authority or administrator, Founding Setup only) — stores the plan and resets its ratifications. Returns `#ok`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`, or `#err(#missingReason)` when the identity recovery procedure is empty.\n" #
    "- `ratifySuccessionPlan(nation) -> RatifySuccessionPlanResult` (update, accepted founding authority only) — records one authority's ratification; when every accepted founding authority has ratified the plan and the constitution, the Nation activates automatically. Returns `#ok`, `#err(#notFoundingAuthority)`, `#err(#duplicateApproval)`, `#err(#planNotRatified)`, or `#err(#notInFoundingSetup)`.\n\n" #
    "### Constitutional amendments and version history\n\n" #
    "An amendment is approved under the constitution currently in effect and never retroactively alters pending decisions or completed votes. The default approval threshold is 75% subject to the constitution's quorum. Ratification produces a new constitution version; the previous version is preserved as history.\n\n" #
    "- `listAmendmentProposals(nation) -> [AmendmentProposal]` (query) — the Nation's amendment proposals with their base version, field-level changes, quorum and approval thresholds, voting deadline, abstention handling and status (`#discussion` / `#voting` / `#ratified` / `#rejected` / `#withdrawn`).\n" #
    "- `listConstitutionVersions(nation) -> [ConstitutionVersion]` (query) — the constitution version history, ordered by version.\n" #
    "- `proposeAmendment(nation, title, summary, changes, votingDeadline) -> SaveAmendmentProposalResult` (update, Nation member) — opens an amendment proposal in `#voting` under the constitution in force. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#missingTitle)`, `#err(#missingSummary)`, `#err(#unknownConstitution)`, or a lifecycle error.\n" #
    "- `ratifyAmendment(nation, proposal) -> RatifyAmendmentResult` (update, accepted founding authority only) — records one authority's ratification; when every accepted founding authority has ratified before the deadline, a new constitution version takes effect. Returns `#ok(versionId)`, `#err(#unknownAmendment)`, `#err(#notFoundingAuthority)`, `#err(#duplicateApproval)`, `#err(#approvalThresholdNotMet)` while more ratifications are needed, `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when the proposal is not open or the deadline has passed, or a lifecycle error.\n\n" #
    "### Dissolution and archiving\n\n" #
    "A constitutionally governed closure workflow with a mandatory cooling-off period, an obligations review, an authorized data export and a final confirmation. **Actual asset settlement and legal dissolution remain outside the simulated functionality**, and closing a digital Nation workspace never implies the dissolution of the Nation, the extinguishment of Indigenous rights or the surrender of sovereignty. An activated Nation can never be deleted unilaterally.\n\n" #
    "- `listDissolutions(nation) -> [Dissolution]` (query) — the Nation's dissolution proposals with their status (`#proposed` / `#coolingOff` / `#voting` / `#approved` / `#archived` / `#rejected` / `#withdrawn`), tally, cooling-off end and archive timestamp.\n" #
    "- `getDissolution(nation) -> ?Dissolution` (query) — the Nation's latest dissolution proposal, or `null`.\n" #
    "- `proposeDissolution(nation, proposal, explanation) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update, Nation member) — opens a dissolution proposal in `#coolingOff`, notifies members and moves the Nation to `#pendingDissolution`. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, `#err(#missingTitle)`, `#err(#missingSummary)`, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when the state does not permit dissolution or one is already live.\n" #
    "- `openDissolutionVoting(nation, dissolution) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update, Nation member) — opens voting once the cooling-off period has elapsed. Returns `#ok(id)` or `#err(#coolingOffNotElapsed)`.\n" #
    "- `castDissolutionVote(nation, dissolution, choice) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update, Nation member) — records one vote (`#inFavor` / `#against` / `#abstain`) in the tally. Returns `#ok(id)`, `#err(#duplicateApproval)` when the member already voted, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` when voting is not open.\n" #
    "- `closeDissolutionVoting(nation, dissolution) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update, Nation member) — closes voting and marks the proposal `#approved` or `#rejected` against its quorum and approval threshold.\n" #
    "- `recordObligationsReview(nation, dissolution, note, outstandingObligations) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update) — records the review of outstanding obligations.\n" #
    "- `recordDataExport(nation, dissolution, reference) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update) — records the authorized data export reference.\n" #
    "- `archiveDissolution(nation, dissolution) -> ArchiveDissolutionResult` (update, an accepted founding authority of the Nation only) — archives the Nation once the proposal is approved, the cooling-off period has elapsed, obligations are reviewed and a data export is recorded. Returns `#ok`, `#err(#alreadyArchived)`, `#err(#coolingOffNotElapsed)`, `#err(#obligationsNotReviewed)`, or `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)`.\n" #
    "- `withdrawDissolution(nation, dissolution) -> SaveDissolutionResult` (update, the proposer only) — withdraws a proposal before archiving and returns the Nation to `#active`.\n" #
    "- `cancelDraftNation(nation) -> ArchiveDissolutionResult` (update, the Nation's authorized creator only) — cancels an unactivated draft or pending-activation Nation. An activated Nation can never be cancelled this way. Returns `#ok`, `#err(#notAuthorized)`, or `#err(#notActivatedDraft)`.\n\n" #
    "### Lifecycle preconditions and retry safety\n\n" #
    "Every continuity mutation consults the Nation's lifecycle state before it runs. Reads of history and records are always allowed in every state. Voting, proposing, recording a departure, emergency suspension and authority changes are permitted in `#active` and `#restrictedGovernance`; admitting a member, amending the constitution and proposing dissolution are permitted only in `#active`; recovery procedures are permitted in `#active` and `#restrictedGovernance`. Founding setup, succession-plan and authority actions run while the Nation is in `#draft` or `#pendingActivation`. `#temporarilySuspended` and `#pendingDissolution` block ordinary governance until restored or resolved, and `#archived` disables operational governance while preserving authorized historical reads. A mutation that is not permitted in the current state returns `#err(#invalidLifecycleTransition)` or `#err(#notAuthorized)` and changes nothing. Every continuity mutation is a single atomic update: a rejected call leaves no partial state, and a retry after a genuine success that allocates a new id creates a duplicate record, so re-read the relevant list before retrying an ambiguous call.\n\n" #
    "### Continuity errors\n\n" #
    "`LifecycleError` is one of `#unknownNation`, `#unknownPosition`, `#unknownAmendment`, `#unknownDeparture`, `#unknownSuspension`, `#unknownDissolution`, `#notAuthorized`, `#notNationMember`, `#notFoundingAuthority`, `#invalidLifecycleTransition`, `#invalidThreshold`, `#quorumNotReached`, `#approvalThresholdNotMet`, `#duplicateApproval`, `#selfApproval`, `#successorNotAccepted`, `#duplicateIdentity`, `#planNotRatified`, `#emergencyScopeExceeded`, `#coolingOffNotElapsed`, `#obligationsNotReviewed`, `#alreadyArchived`, `#notActivatedDraft`, `#missingReason`, `#missingTitle` or `#missingSummary`. Every continuity mutation returns one of these instead of trapping, so a caller can correct and retry. Each successful create call allocates a new id (not idempotent); a retry after a network error creates a duplicate record.\n\n" #
    "## Units and encodings\n\n" #
    "- All timestamps (`timestamp`, `openTimestamp`, `closeTimestamp`, `lockStart`, `unlockTime`) are `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, exactly `Time.now()`'s native unit — convert to milliseconds by dividing by 1,000,000 on the client.\n" #
    "- SRC amounts, treasury amounts, and token allocation amounts are plain `Nat`; none of them carry an implied decimal scaling or currency. Nation treasury `amount` values are the same plain `Nat` units, chosen by the community, with no implied currency or decimal scaling.\n" #
    "- `lockTermSeconds` is seconds, not nanoseconds; `maturityRateBps` is basis points (1/100 of a percent) of `lockedAmount`.\n" #
    "- Optional fields (`?T`) are `null` until set — e.g. a `Contribution`'s `reviewer` / `rationale` / `srcAwarded` stay `null` until a reviewer acts on it.\n\n" #
    "## Object Query Layer (OQL)\n\n" #
    "`schema()` / `execute()` expose `contribution`, `assignment`, `srcTransaction`, `treasuryTransaction`, `proposal`, `vote`, `voteDelegation`, `stakingRecord`, `waitlistEntry`, `challengeImpression`, `challengeStart`, `challengeResponse`, `publicComment`, `commentReport`, `lead`, `communityProfile`, `discoverySubmission`, `pipelineItem`, `pipelineInteraction`, `collaborationProfile`, `introductionRequest`, `networkActivity`, `nation`, `workspace`, `workspaceApp`, `nationProposal`, `discussionThread`, `discussionPost`, `nationMember`, `nationDocument`, `calendarEvent`, `nationTreasuryTransaction`, `privacySettings`, `networkNationProfile`, `nationOwnership`, `nationTheme`, `nationMembershipVoting`, `nationFolder`, `nationFile`, `fileAttachment`, `constitution`, `amendment`, `governanceRole`, `roleAssignment`, `roleDelegation`, `governanceProposal`, `governanceVote`, `executionRequest`, `executionAudit`, `appeal`, `censusEntry`, `joinRequest`, `membershipInvitation`, `memberAdmission`, `recordedVote`, `governanceHistory`, `memberDeparture`, `emergencySuspension`, `nationLifecycle`, `authorityPosition`, `authorityTermEvent`, `successionPlan`, `constitutionVersion`, `amendmentProposal`, `dissolution`, `foundingSetup` and `foundingAppointment` as queryable tables for the Data Intelligence agent, each with its own per-table authorization (public tables for treasury/proposal/vote/delegation transparency, public comments, community profiles, pipeline items and interactions, collaboration profiles, the network activity feed, and the Nation listing, workspace registry and SOVEREIGN Network profiles; owner-scoped-with-controller-oversight for contributions, assignments, SRC transactions and discovery submissions; strictly owner-scoped for staking records; controller-only for waitlist submissions, the pseudonymous participation events, comment reports, lead records, introduction requests, the Nation workspace content — proposals, discussions, members, documents, calendar, treasury, privacy settings, ownership records, visual themes, membership/voting configuration, and the Nation Files tables `nationFolder`, `nationFile` and `fileAttachment` — and the Nation governance tables `constitution`, `amendment`, `governanceRole`, `roleAssignment`, `roleDelegation`, `governanceProposal`, `governanceVote`, `executionRequest`, `executionAudit`, `appeal`, `censusEntry`, `joinRequest`, `membershipInvitation`, `memberAdmission`, `recordedVote`, `governanceHistory`, `memberDeparture`, `emergencySuspension`, `nationLifecycle`, `authorityPosition`, `authorityTermEvent`, `successionPlan`, `constitutionVersion`, `amendmentProposal`, `dissolution`, `foundingSetup` and `foundingAppointment`). The `nationFile` table exposes file metadata (`name`, `size`, `contentType`, `uploadedBy`, `folder`, `timestamp`) but not the off-chain content reference, which is an opaque blob handle rather than queryable data. The governance tables project variant fields as Text tags and omit nested rule sets and evidence arrays, which are not supported OQL column types. These are read-only query tables layered over the same state as the methods above — they do not change any lifecycle or authorization rule described in this document.\n\n" #
    "## Errors and non-obvious gotchas\n\n" #
    "- Every `Runtime.trap(...)` in this backend rolls back the whole call; no partial state change is left behind by a trapped update.\n" #
    "- `tokenomics` writes return `Result<(), Text>` instead of trapping on a bad submission specifically so a caller can retry with corrected numbers without losing other in-flight work.\n" #
    "- `getTreasurySummary().runwayMonths == null` means there is no recent expense history to project a burn rate from — it is never a signal of infinite runway.\n" #
    "- Assignment status `#queuedAwaitingFunding` is a transparency label only; nothing in this backend automatically checks treasury funds before an admin calls `advanceAssignmentStatus`.";
  };
};
